    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d701">

                <pb facs="0628" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg512"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 033.1100K77/35.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of Guatemala to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of Guatemala</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 19, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have received your
                    kind letter of February 13th, 1912,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d701-f1"/> and take
                    pleasure in informing you that we shall be more than pleased to have his
                    excellency the Secretary of State, Mr. Knox, with us, also his distinguished
                    wife, and all the members of the party accompanying them, and to further show my
                    pleasure I will leave tonight to be present at a reception which we are to give
                    in honor of Mr. and Mrs. Knox in Guatemala.</p>
                <p>Every effort will be made to make the visit of Mr. Knox a most happy one, a visit
                    that will, I am sure, make the relations more intimate, as I have had the
                    pleasure to assure you in my official letter of February 12th, 1912.</p>
                <p>Officially, and personally, I wish to state that the decision of His Excellency
                    President Taft has been received by the Guatemalan Government and people as a
                    high honor.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joaquín Méndez.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d701-f1" n="1" xml:id="d701-f1-content">
                <p>The identic letter printed under Panama: “Visit of the Secretary of State to the
